WEBVTT

00:14.110 --> 00:16.840
[Xucheng]

00:30.640 --> 00:31.900
It's come back to life!

00:32.150 --> 00:33.410
It's come back to life!

00:35.790 --> 00:38.520
Do we really have to play dead
to get into the city?

00:39.390 --> 00:41.100
The living have to pay a head tax
to enter the city.

00:41.100 --> 00:42.430
This way, it's cheaper.

00:50.070 --> 00:53.320
I haven't heard of any plague
or bandit attack in this city.

00:53.320 --> 00:54.920
What exactly happened here?

01:02.430 --> 01:03.640
No fracture to the neck.

01:03.640 --> 01:05.060
The face has turned bluish-purple.

01:05.060 --> 01:07.390
Judging by the angle
of the ligature mark,

01:07.480 --> 01:09.560
the airway was compressed,
causing death by suffocation.

01:09.560 --> 01:10.620
This was a suicide.

01:11.310 --> 01:12.840
That one slit their wrists.

01:13.310 --> 01:14.560
What could've happened

01:14.560 --> 01:15.760
to make so many people

01:17.090 --> 01:18.950
kill themselves at the same time?

01:39.680 --> 01:40.680
Just like the last one,

01:40.680 --> 01:41.880
this was suicide too.

01:46.210 --> 01:47.650
What does this symbol mean?

01:47.650 --> 01:49.310
It's a death symbol used here.

01:49.350 --> 01:50.640
If a whole family dies,

01:50.759 --> 01:52.759
they mark the wall with this symbol.

01:53.000 --> 01:54.220
Looks like the situation in Xucheng

01:54.220 --> 01:55.950
is even worse than we imagined.

02:01.540 --> 02:03.270
The smell of burning bodies...

02:18.530 --> 02:19.250
Mom...

02:20.780 --> 02:21.500
Mom...

02:22.800 --> 02:23.360
Take her back.

02:23.360 --> 02:24.120
Mom.

02:25.370 --> 02:26.090
Mom!

02:33.650 --> 02:35.710
Those lackeys from the Governor's Office

02:35.710 --> 02:37.120
will get what's coming to them
sooner or later.

02:37.120 --> 02:39.400
Yeah. They're worse than beasts.

02:39.900 --> 02:41.060
These people have no regard
for human life.

02:41.060 --> 02:42.000
What a tragedy.

02:50.750 --> 02:52.090
I'm telling you, there's something off
about that Balai Ancient God.

02:52.090 --> 02:53.120
That thing isn't human at all.

02:53.120 --> 02:53.690
Sir,

02:55.250 --> 02:56.810
my parents are both dead.

02:57.520 --> 02:59.090
They made me burn the bodies,

02:59.090 --> 02:59.579
but I was too scared,

02:59.579 --> 03:00.460
so they beat me.

03:01.130 --> 03:02.370
My brother and I just got back
from out of town—

03:02.370 --> 03:03.480
we have no idea what's going on.

03:03.480 --> 03:05.280
Could you tell us what happened?

03:05.900 --> 03:06.740
Some time ago,

03:06.970 --> 03:08.460
someone brought Governor Herman

03:08.460 --> 03:10.620
a Balinese statue
they found on the beach.

03:10.620 --> 03:12.530
After that, the governor slowly changed.

03:12.530 --> 03:14.460
He started ordering us

03:14.460 --> 03:15.460
to smash all the other statues,

03:15.460 --> 03:17.590
saying his Balai Ancient God
didn't like them.

03:17.590 --> 03:18.950
If anyone dared worship another god,

03:18.950 --> 03:19.810
he'd kill them.

03:20.000 --> 03:22.020
That Balinese statue is said
to be extremely eerie.

03:22.020 --> 03:24.710
My sister-in-law works as a maid
in the Governor's Office.

03:24.710 --> 03:26.020
She said things get really strange

03:26.020 --> 03:27.020
at night there...

03:27.300 --> 03:28.480
It can even talk.

03:29.020 --> 03:31.579
Mei...

03:34.190 --> 03:36.520
But what does
this Balai Ancient God being able to talk

03:36.520 --> 03:38.450
have to do with burning my parents?

03:38.460 --> 03:40.190
After the city
started worshipping the new god,

03:40.190 --> 03:41.870
the governor ordered everyone

03:41.870 --> 03:43.620
to pray to that Balai Ancient God.

03:43.620 --> 03:44.390
After

03:45.110 --> 03:46.079
worshipping it for a while,

03:46.079 --> 03:49.000
people started hearing
the Balai Ancient God's voice.

03:49.000 --> 03:49.920
The voice

03:49.950 --> 03:52.410
kept telling them
to find some strange cave.

03:52.579 --> 03:54.710
A lot of people thought
it was a divine calling,

03:54.710 --> 03:56.450
so they all went looking for the cave.

03:56.450 --> 03:57.310
Some people went mad

03:57.310 --> 03:59.250
because they couldn't endure the voice,

03:59.250 --> 04:01.870
and in the end, they couldn't hold on
any longer and killed themselves.

04:01.870 --> 04:02.520
The governor said

04:02.520 --> 04:03.920
those people were traitors—

04:03.920 --> 04:05.250
they were to be burned alive,

04:05.250 --> 04:07.450
and their bodies completely cremated.

04:07.450 --> 04:08.810
Thank you, sir.

04:08.840 --> 04:09.740
Keep your voice down.

04:09.740 --> 04:10.670
They'll hear us.

04:11.210 --> 04:12.030
Looks like this Balai Ancient God

04:12.030 --> 04:13.290
isn't the one I blew up.

04:13.510 --> 04:15.570
Feels more like its brother, though.

04:15.630 --> 04:16.870
There's definitely more than one.

04:16.870 --> 04:19.000
Didn't we already see several of them?

04:19.779 --> 04:20.589
So,

04:21.940 --> 04:23.230
wanna check it out while we're here?

04:23.230 --> 04:26.060
Seems like Governor Herman's
under that thing's spell.

04:26.060 --> 04:26.690
How about

04:26.980 --> 04:29.240
we save the people from their suffering?

04:29.480 --> 04:30.660
Funny, you sound

04:31.000 --> 04:33.060
pretty familiar
with this Governor Herman guy.

04:33.060 --> 04:34.330
You could say we're "medium rare."

04:34.330 --> 04:35.659
Herman's a real piece of work.

04:35.659 --> 04:37.770
I've got a bit
of personal history with him.

04:37.770 --> 04:38.250
Yeah,

04:38.250 --> 04:39.050
you seem to have personal history

04:39.050 --> 04:40.420
with even the dogs at the door.

04:40.420 --> 04:42.880
Holding grudges is basically your hobby.

04:42.909 --> 04:44.040
Hey, don't say that—

04:44.500 --> 04:46.500
it's about my country and my family.

04:52.800 --> 04:53.450
Shrimpie,

04:54.360 --> 04:56.560
I recently learned a few new disguises.

04:56.950 --> 04:57.690
See

04:58.360 --> 04:59.690
if there's one you like.

05:02.100 --> 05:03.160
Give me 10 minutes.

05:06.120 --> 05:07.100
While investigating the case recently,

05:07.100 --> 05:08.110
I heard a scandal

05:08.540 --> 05:09.750
about Governor Herman—

05:09.750 --> 05:11.550
he has a thing for Chinese girls.

05:26.600 --> 05:27.580
Try this one.

05:36.690 --> 05:38.580
♪ Hey there, hey there, sweet hey there ♪

05:39.020 --> 05:41.500
♪ Hey there, hey there, sweet hey there ♪

05:39.360 --> 05:40.560
You really nailed it.

05:42.070 --> 05:42.930
Almost forgot.

05:43.700 --> 05:46.350
♪ Hey there, hey there, sweet hey there ♪

05:46.480 --> 05:49.850
[Golden Needle—Special Equipment
of the Archives; Voice Modulation]

05:46.850 --> 05:47.880
♪ With harmony we make our way
through the world ♪

05:48.450 --> 05:49.170
♪ Or lose an arm in the name of justice ♪

05:49.630 --> 05:51.250
♪ Breaking through the maze,
I still dare to carry on ♪

05:55.770 --> 05:58.430
♪ Hey there, hey there, sweet hey there ♪

05:57.480 --> 05:59.270
Mentor taught us all kinds of skills,

05:58.940 --> 06:00.000
♪ With harmony we make our way
through the world ♪

05:59.680 --> 06:01.040
but when it comes to human-skin masks,

06:00.230 --> 06:01.240
♪ Or lose an arm in the name of justice ♪

06:01.660 --> 06:03.180
♪ Breaking through the maze,
I still dare to carry on ♪

06:01.870 --> 06:03.730
no one makes them better than you.

06:04.160 --> 06:04.890
Of course.

07:29.160 --> 07:35.240
[Archives: The Nanyang Mystery]

07:35.650 --> 07:38.340
[Episode 2]

07:53.630 --> 07:54.630
Stop right there.

07:54.690 --> 07:56.020
What are you doing here?

07:57.250 --> 07:58.980
Governor Herman's arrangement.

07:58.980 --> 08:00.040
Don't ask too much.

08:01.420 --> 08:03.140
But you look a bit buff.

08:04.110 --> 08:05.580
Why don't you

08:05.600 --> 08:07.600
come inside with me

08:07.790 --> 08:10.850
and let him explain to you himself?
Step aside, please.

08:14.480 --> 08:15.770
We'll split up in a bit.

08:24.040 --> 08:24.800
Come on in.

08:25.830 --> 08:27.160
What are you doing here?

08:27.800 --> 08:30.200
Your excellency, today's goods delivery.

08:34.500 --> 08:36.159
Who asked you to deliver this?

08:36.289 --> 08:37.100
Get out.

08:37.340 --> 08:38.409
Then I'll take her away.

08:38.409 --> 08:39.169
Wait.

08:40.169 --> 08:40.860
Leave her,

08:41.340 --> 08:41.770
and go.

08:41.980 --> 08:42.409
Okay.

09:31.370 --> 09:33.530
The governor sent me to make an offering
to the Balai Ancient God.

09:33.530 --> 09:34.100
May I ask

09:34.550 --> 09:36.880
where the Balai Ancient God
is enshrined?

09:38.840 --> 09:39.720
Follow me.

09:52.170 --> 09:53.130
It's right here.

09:53.410 --> 09:54.720
You can go in by yourself.

09:54.720 --> 09:55.980
I'm not going in there.

10:23.530 --> 10:26.630
Go there.

10:27.860 --> 10:29.620
There,

10:30.320 --> 10:35.250
you'll have everything
you've ever wanted.

10:39.080 --> 10:39.870
So,

10:40.220 --> 10:41.340
what's your name?

10:47.770 --> 10:49.300
I like a woman who's feisty.

10:51.770 --> 10:54.390
I ask, and you answer.

10:54.620 --> 10:56.350
If it's incorrect, you'll die.

10:57.980 --> 10:59.860
What did the Balinese statue

10:59.860 --> 11:01.280
tell you to do?

11:01.700 --> 11:04.340
It's forcing me
to find some mysterious cave.

11:06.010 --> 11:07.860
Is it under a salt marsh?

11:07.940 --> 11:08.480
Yes.

11:08.510 --> 11:09.710
A creepy place.

11:09.730 --> 11:11.220
I brought a bunch of people there.

11:11.220 --> 11:13.080
A lot of them died.

11:19.370 --> 11:20.720
Shh...

11:28.940 --> 11:32.820
Next question.
Who gave the Balinese statue to you?

11:32.820 --> 11:34.440
This Chinese person

11:34.620 --> 11:35.840
is an officer.

11:35.840 --> 11:37.580
It's all I know. It's all I know.

11:40.600 --> 11:42.630
What happened to those Eastern girls

11:42.630 --> 11:44.030
you brought here before?

11:44.170 --> 11:45.240
I let them go...

11:45.410 --> 11:46.980
Dead. They're dead.

11:46.980 --> 11:48.200
How did they die?

11:49.720 --> 11:52.080
They just couldn't, you know, take it

11:52.440 --> 11:53.910
and the next day...

12:18.920 --> 12:20.580
I didn't expect you could talk.

12:20.580 --> 12:22.180
Guess I underestimated you.

12:22.560 --> 12:23.370
No... wait.

12:23.860 --> 12:25.160
Your brother's already buried

12:25.160 --> 12:27.110
at the bottom of that cave.

12:27.280 --> 12:28.530
You're the next one.

12:32.650 --> 12:35.270
Have you ever thought
about the people around you?

12:35.270 --> 12:36.330
You're satisfied,

12:37.100 --> 12:38.760
but what about everyone else?

12:38.770 --> 12:40.570
Not everyone is as strong as you.

12:40.910 --> 12:42.640
Some people just can't take it.

12:44.500 --> 12:45.940
I can't take you with me,

12:46.170 --> 12:47.290
but I can't leave you here

12:47.290 --> 12:48.550
to harm others either.

12:49.030 --> 12:50.560
Shrimpie, what should I do?

12:57.580 --> 12:59.910
Why don't I just finish you off
right here?

13:01.340 --> 13:07.100
[Young Woman Murdered]
[Urgent: Missing Person]

13:10.330 --> 13:11.320
[Young Woman Murdered]

13:56.410 --> 13:57.740
Why did you switch back?

13:58.010 --> 14:00.340
We might still need it later
when we go out.

14:01.170 --> 14:02.700
Then I'll leave this part to you
next time.

14:02.700 --> 14:03.560
What happened?

14:03.940 --> 14:05.050
I've done my part.

14:05.740 --> 14:06.600
I meant her.

14:06.860 --> 14:08.260
What's going on with her?

14:14.290 --> 14:16.340
Her parents were bewitched
by the Evil God.

14:16.340 --> 14:17.540
She became an orphan,

14:18.170 --> 14:20.430
and then Herman sent his men to seize her.

14:20.940 --> 14:22.200
If I hadn't come today,

14:23.600 --> 14:25.060
she would've been killed.

14:33.660 --> 14:35.060
Did you find the Evil God?

14:35.580 --> 14:36.370
I did.

14:37.220 --> 14:39.290
The one he worships is also
one of those Balai evil gods,

14:39.290 --> 14:40.860
just not the same one

14:40.860 --> 14:41.740
beneath the salt marsh.

14:41.740 --> 14:42.580
To be safe,

14:42.580 --> 14:43.940
I destroyed it on the spot

14:43.940 --> 14:46.540
so it wouldn't harm anyone again
in the future.

14:52.620 --> 14:53.770
I sealed off all the windows

14:53.770 --> 14:55.230
and set the statue on fire.

14:58.530 --> 15:00.390
What did you find out from Herman?

15:02.750 --> 15:05.950
The Evil God statue was given to him
by a military officer.

15:06.790 --> 15:08.410
All the leads

15:08.410 --> 15:09.670
point back to the army.

15:22.580 --> 15:24.220
Fire! Somebody help!

15:29.220 --> 15:30.860
What exactly did you do?

15:33.980 --> 15:36.640
I just did a little more
than what was asked of me.

15:40.170 --> 15:40.750
Water!

15:41.080 --> 15:42.170
Put in the water!

15:42.170 --> 15:43.050
Come on!

15:44.000 --> 15:44.820
Hurry up!

15:45.500 --> 15:46.340
Are you okay?

15:46.340 --> 15:47.870
It's fine. Don't be afraid.

15:53.010 --> 15:54.010
Isn't this great?

15:54.650 --> 15:55.620
Herman is dead,

15:55.720 --> 15:56.850
the Evil God is gone,

15:57.290 --> 15:59.340
and the innocent people are finally free.

15:59.340 --> 16:00.740
Our mission is complete—

16:00.890 --> 16:02.690
we've prevented this disaster.

16:12.510 --> 16:13.910
Alright, I admit…

16:14.750 --> 16:16.480
I really didn't expect the fire

16:17.790 --> 16:18.600
to

16:19.420 --> 16:20.330
get that big.

16:20.480 --> 16:21.880
I'll do better next time.

16:23.200 --> 16:24.710
But we were the last ones out.

16:24.710 --> 16:25.310
I checked—

16:25.960 --> 16:27.420
no civilians were harmed.

16:29.510 --> 16:30.240
Then care

16:30.240 --> 16:31.500
to explain something to me?

16:31.500 --> 16:34.500
Why leave before the Evil God statue
was fully burned?

16:35.670 --> 16:36.750
How do you explain

16:37.670 --> 16:38.790
a fire like that?

16:39.260 --> 16:40.130
Mr. Shrimp,

16:40.650 --> 16:42.470
I honestly didn't see this coming.

16:42.470 --> 16:45.530
I mean… it's a stone building—
how did it burn like that?

16:48.480 --> 16:49.460
Sorry,

16:49.910 --> 16:51.150
I'll be more careful next time.

16:51.150 --> 16:51.950
More careful.

16:53.360 --> 16:54.220
You always

16:54.500 --> 16:56.520
take things to 99%,

16:57.370 --> 16:59.370
but you never cross the finish line.

17:01.750 --> 17:02.440
Look,

17:05.030 --> 17:06.290
It's dying down. It's dying down.

17:06.290 --> 17:07.609
Look. It's fine.

17:09.430 --> 17:10.109
Come on,

17:10.790 --> 17:12.270
don't be such a perfectionist—

17:12.270 --> 17:14.270
leave yourself a little room to improve.

17:14.270 --> 17:15.530
So, what's for dinner?

17:17.849 --> 17:19.270
I'm getting roast chicken.

17:19.270 --> 17:20.329
You're not allowed to eat—

17:20.329 --> 17:22.230
you stay here and reflect.

17:22.349 --> 17:23.040
No way.

17:23.530 --> 17:25.720
I got 99% of the job done,

17:26.030 --> 17:27.640
so I should get 99% of the roast chicken.

17:27.640 --> 17:29.660
Just dock me 1% and feed that part
to a dog, alright?

17:29.660 --> 17:31.990
But I still have to write
an honest report.

17:34.000 --> 17:36.070
We've completed the mission, haven't we?

17:36.070 --> 17:36.820
We can get probationary approval now.

17:36.820 --> 17:38.660
There are still
many mysteries unresolved.

17:38.660 --> 17:40.030
How are we supposed to close the case?

17:40.030 --> 17:41.110
What mysteries?

17:41.720 --> 17:42.720
Governor Herman is dead,

17:42.720 --> 17:43.750
the Evil God statue is burned,

17:43.750 --> 17:45.400
and the Xucheng crisis is over.

17:45.400 --> 17:47.460
People here can live normally again.

17:49.160 --> 17:50.940
As for that Evil God…

17:51.310 --> 17:53.250
strange things happen

17:53.250 --> 17:54.770
all the time in Nanyang anyway.

17:54.770 --> 17:55.920
Just write this:

17:56.480 --> 17:58.810
Nanyang's so hot it drove everyone crazy.

18:18.520 --> 18:21.330
[Zhang Haiqi,
Director of the Southern Archives]

18:21.340 --> 18:23.830
[Zhang Hailou, Mentor of Zhang Haixia]

18:23.850 --> 18:26.320
[Special Attribute: Slow Aging]

18:32.550 --> 18:33.880
What are you looking at?

18:37.040 --> 18:38.100
I'm talking to you.

19:05.570 --> 19:06.340
Mentor.

19:07.210 --> 19:07.960
Mentor.

19:08.560 --> 19:09.830
what are you doing in Nanyang?

19:09.830 --> 19:11.030
Are you here to see us?

19:15.500 --> 19:16.630
What does this mean?

19:17.630 --> 19:19.000
Well, long time no see.

19:19.050 --> 19:20.710
You've gotten quite capable.

19:21.250 --> 19:24.050
You even dared to burn down
the Governor's Office?

19:24.740 --> 19:25.850
I was investigating the case!

19:25.850 --> 19:27.670
I was saving innocent lives!

19:30.330 --> 19:31.790
Zhang Haixia can testify!

19:36.850 --> 19:37.610
Mentor,

19:37.920 --> 19:39.720
the investigation part is true,

19:40.140 --> 19:41.090
but this is the first time

19:41.090 --> 19:43.700
I've heard anything about
"saving innocent lives."

19:43.700 --> 19:44.620
How could you just stand by
and do nothing?

19:44.620 --> 19:46.480
Zhang Haixia, you're his senior.

19:46.550 --> 19:47.240
Failing to keep him in check

19:47.240 --> 19:48.370
is also punishable.

19:48.660 --> 19:50.390
Come up here and grill the fish.

19:51.050 --> 19:51.700
Yes.

19:54.250 --> 19:54.720
Wait—

19:55.210 --> 19:56.250
why does he get to grill fish

19:56.250 --> 19:57.310
while I'm left here

20:02.050 --> 20:02.680
drowning?

20:06.330 --> 20:07.810
Why does he go up to grill fish

20:07.810 --> 20:09.470
while I'm left here drowning?

20:10.380 --> 20:11.380
Let me ask you—

20:11.980 --> 20:13.810
what did I tell you

20:13.980 --> 20:15.140
when I first took you in?

20:15.140 --> 20:16.740
Who the hell remembers that?

20:19.180 --> 20:21.240
Then go to hell and try to remember it.

20:28.920 --> 20:29.550
What?

20:30.330 --> 20:31.660
You want to join him too?

20:38.380 --> 20:39.480
I remember.

20:39.530 --> 20:40.560
I remember—

20:40.940 --> 20:43.070
you told me to overcome my true nature.

20:47.250 --> 20:49.850
Zhang Hailou, remember this.

20:53.330 --> 20:54.960
And congratulations—

20:55.270 --> 20:56.730
you've passed probation.

20:57.250 --> 20:58.050
We've passed?

20:59.110 --> 21:00.740
You can consider
your mission accomplished.

21:00.740 --> 21:02.600
So you've passed your probation.

21:02.640 --> 21:04.770
The rest will be handed over to others.

21:05.180 --> 21:08.110
There will be more urgent cases
assigned to you soon.

21:09.420 --> 21:11.090
So we're not
investigating that case anymore?

21:11.090 --> 21:13.160
If Mentor says it's done,
then it's done.

21:13.160 --> 21:14.420
No more questions.

21:16.820 --> 21:17.400
Go

21:17.880 --> 21:19.080
get me some more wine.

21:19.660 --> 21:20.440
We're celebrating

21:20.440 --> 21:22.090
your official entry into the Archives.

21:22.090 --> 21:23.090
I'm happy today—

21:23.510 --> 21:25.840
I want Nanyang's perak pearl wine.

21:26.570 --> 21:28.630
Drink too much and you'll age faster.

21:29.550 --> 21:30.310
And you too.

21:30.710 --> 21:32.630
I had nothing to do with it, Mentor.

21:32.630 --> 21:33.430
Zhang Hailou,

21:34.030 --> 21:35.090
stand right there.

21:35.420 --> 21:36.620
You two little brats!

21:38.280 --> 21:38.960
[Nanyang Maritime
Supervisory Office]

21:38.980 --> 21:40.810
[Southern Archives,
Balongzhou Branch]

21:40.910 --> 21:43.470
[Award of Commendation]

21:41.790 --> 21:43.380
Now that you've become full members,

21:43.380 --> 21:46.070
you must follow the rules
of the Archives even more strictly.

21:46.070 --> 21:46.720
First,

21:47.180 --> 21:49.290
the Archives
is a top-secret organization.

21:49.290 --> 21:53.220
In public, you are commissioners
of the Maritime Supervisory Office.

22:00.250 --> 22:00.790
Second,

22:01.400 --> 22:02.250
your duties

22:02.250 --> 22:03.680
also include assisting the government

22:03.680 --> 22:06.140
in capturing certain dangerous criminals.

22:06.760 --> 22:10.360
[Donggang Pirate Execution Case]

22:09.070 --> 22:09.610
Third,

22:10.380 --> 22:12.110
if the two of you ever disagree,

22:12.570 --> 22:13.570
listen to Haixia.

22:50.320 --> 22:53.590
[Xihang Black Ship Massacre Case]

22:51.330 --> 22:51.980
Don't kill me…

22:51.980 --> 22:53.580
Don't kill me… Don't kill me…

23:01.000 --> 23:01.750
Don't kill me.

23:01.750 --> 23:02.550
Don't kill me.

23:17.220 --> 23:17.790
Plague…

23:18.000 --> 23:19.000
the Sea Plague.

23:27.780 --> 23:28.180
[Zhang Hailou a.k.a. Zhang Salty]

23:28.200 --> 23:28.600
[Sea Plague,
Nanyang's Number One Bladesman

23:28.660 --> 23:29.260
[Physical: 185 cm, 64 kg]

23:29.290 --> 23:29.880
[Tall and Straight Posture.
Heart on the Right Side]

23:29.970 --> 23:31.220
[Personality: Eccentric, Uninhibited,
Reckless, Unfiltered]

23:31.480 --> 23:32.500
[Zhang Haixia
a.k.a. Zhang Shrimpie, Shrimpie]

23:32.520 --> 23:33.250
[Physical: Handsome]

23:33.290 --> 23:34.090
[Personality: Calm, Composed,
Meticulous, Thorough]

23:34.110 --> 23:34.940
[Intelligent, Lively, Caring, Warm]

23:34.960 --> 23:35.530
[Ability: Keen Sense of Smell]

23:35.560 --> 23:36.370
[Voice Mimicry, Disguise,
and Strong Swimmer]

23:37.310 --> 23:38.010
In 7 years,

23:38.480 --> 23:40.330
they wiped out bandits and pirates,

23:40.330 --> 23:42.050
keeping peace across Nanyang.

23:41.010 --> 23:43.160
[Nanyang Maritime
Supervisory Office]

23:42.700 --> 23:43.500
Zhang Hailou,

23:44.000 --> 23:45.160
due to his extreme methods

23:45.160 --> 23:46.200
in carrying out missions,

23:46.200 --> 23:47.830
became the dreaded

23:48.070 --> 23:51.600
"Sea Plague" feared by pirates
and revered by civilians alike.

23:51.850 --> 23:53.710
Calm and collected, Zhang Haixia

23:53.900 --> 23:56.010
earned repeated victories

23:56.010 --> 23:57.350
through his impeccable judgment

23:57.350 --> 23:59.750
and became highly valued by his superiors.

23:59.850 --> 24:01.220
Yet what they did not know was

24:00.320 --> 24:04.760
[Nanyang Maritime
Supervisory Office]

24:02.000 --> 24:05.400
that the forces behind the Evil God Case
were still making their moves.

24:05.400 --> 24:07.330
A case that would change their fate

24:07.460 --> 24:08.590
was about to unfold—

24:09.720 --> 24:11.350
the Panhua Reef Case.

24:23.110 --> 24:24.510
May the heavens bless us—

24:24.530 --> 24:26.740
may this voyage be safe and uneventful.

24:27.690 --> 24:29.090
May the heavens bless us—

24:29.290 --> 24:30.680
may this voyage

24:30.920 --> 24:32.270
be safe and uneventful.

24:33.070 --> 24:34.470
May the heavens bless us—

24:34.960 --> 24:36.330
may this voyage

24:36.570 --> 24:37.940
be safe and uneventful.

24:38.750 --> 24:40.150
May the heavens bless us—

24:40.420 --> 24:41.640
may this voyage

24:41.940 --> 24:43.270
be safe and uneventful.

24:47.920 --> 24:48.420
Bing,

24:48.770 --> 24:49.770
fog's rolling in.

24:51.000 --> 24:51.480
Bing,

24:51.980 --> 24:53.310
heavy fog's rolling in!

24:58.680 --> 24:59.980
Bing, come quickly!

25:01.610 --> 25:02.460
What's going on?

25:02.460 --> 25:03.960
It looks like there's someone out there.

25:03.960 --> 25:04.880
Don't talk nonsense.

25:04.880 --> 25:06.400
How could there be anyone this far
out at sea?

25:06.400 --> 25:07.830
Look—see?

25:14.070 --> 25:15.680
Heavens, please protect us...

25:15.680 --> 25:17.610
We're just trying to make a living.

25:18.010 --> 25:19.350
Please spare us...

25:22.410 --> 25:23.230
Ghost!

25:23.400 --> 25:24.660
Bing, hurry, let's go!

25:24.770 --> 25:25.420
Go!

25:32.070 --> 25:32.700
Bing!

25:35.790 --> 25:36.440
Bing!

25:36.810 --> 25:37.770
Bing!

25:53.240 --> 25:55.600
[Nanyang Maritime
Supervisory Office]

25:55.720 --> 26:03.920
[Maritime Supervisory Office]

25:58.740 --> 25:59.350
Sir.

25:59.880 --> 26:00.610
T-This…

26:01.180 --> 26:02.500
I came to file a report…

26:02.660 --> 26:03.860
W-What place is this?

26:06.090 --> 26:12.120
[Maritime Supervisory Office]

26:06.810 --> 26:09.200
Shrimpie, where did you hide
my cigarettes this time?

26:09.200 --> 26:10.460
Where did you put them?

26:12.050 --> 26:12.980
Alright, got it.

26:16.420 --> 26:21.670
[Maritime Supervisory Office]

26:17.090 --> 26:18.420
His name is Chen Libiao.

26:18.420 --> 26:19.940
He was sent by the higher-ups
to file a report—

26:19.940 --> 26:22.340
said he encountered a ghost
at Panhua Reef.

26:23.740 --> 26:24.770
Panhua Reef?

26:25.330 --> 26:27.160
Haven't ships stopped
passing through there for a long time?

26:27.160 --> 26:27.740
Yeah.

26:27.940 --> 26:29.960
There've been rumors that Panhua Reef
is haunted by water ghosts lately,

26:29.960 --> 26:31.770
so most ships refuse
to pass through there.

26:31.770 --> 26:33.050
But there are still bold ones

26:33.050 --> 26:35.510
trying to get rich
by salvaging shipwrecks.

26:35.810 --> 26:38.470
We've already had 7 similar reports
this month.

26:39.160 --> 26:41.620
The previous reports
were all just hearsay—

26:42.260 --> 26:44.390
but this time, there's an actual body.

26:54.220 --> 26:55.980
Why didn't you listen to me?

26:58.180 --> 26:59.310
Who is the deceased?

26:59.650 --> 27:00.510
Go into detail.

27:04.330 --> 27:06.810
We saw ghosts at Panhua Reef.

27:08.610 --> 27:10.850
Bing was killed by a water ghost.

27:29.050 --> 27:30.310
It's salt.

27:30.890 --> 27:32.790
His belly is stuffed full of salt.

27:33.250 --> 27:34.890
It's the first time

27:35.200 --> 27:36.680
I've seen someone killed

27:37.210 --> 27:38.210
by being pickled.

27:44.750 --> 27:45.880
Let's go take a look.

27:47.550 --> 27:50.740
Move the body down
and secure it properly. Prepare the ship—

27:50.740 --> 27:53.070
we leave for Panhua Reef at dawn tomorrow.

27:54.810 --> 27:55.900
Easy there…

27:57.880 --> 27:58.680
Hey, don't go—

27:59.740 --> 28:00.630
you're supposed to lead the way.

28:00.630 --> 28:01.770
No, I'm not going.

28:02.810 --> 28:04.440
Sir, please… I'm begging you,

28:04.440 --> 28:05.580
Sir, I dare not go.

28:05.600 --> 28:06.190
Wait!

28:15.610 --> 28:16.410
Wait outside.

28:21.460 --> 28:23.060
What do you think about this?

28:25.350 --> 28:27.350
The appearance of the body at this time

28:27.350 --> 28:28.440
is highly suspicious.

28:28.440 --> 28:30.160
A large passenger ship has been missing

28:30.160 --> 28:31.440
in this sea area for a year.

28:31.440 --> 28:33.770
The so-called "water ghost"
has always been nothing but rumors—

28:33.770 --> 28:35.110
never any evidence.

28:35.680 --> 28:36.960
But now there's a corpse,

28:36.960 --> 28:38.490
and there's also a witness.

28:39.530 --> 28:40.500
I think something must

28:40.500 --> 28:42.030
have happened on that reef.

28:43.340 --> 28:46.000
An isolated island,
surrounded by endless sea—

28:46.530 --> 28:49.190
no matter how skilled we are,
it won't be worth a damn.

28:49.190 --> 28:50.450
This is indeed tricky.

28:52.700 --> 28:54.100
Have you ever considered

28:54.580 --> 28:56.220
that we don't have to investigate it?

28:56.220 --> 28:57.830
We could just report it
to headquarters directly.

28:57.830 --> 28:58.630
And then what?

28:58.880 --> 29:00.030
Open a little shop,

29:00.270 --> 29:01.530
make some small money,

29:01.830 --> 29:04.090
and spend the rest of our lives like that?

29:04.550 --> 29:05.460
Do you still remember

29:05.460 --> 29:06.830
the case we handled beneath a salt marsh—

29:06.830 --> 29:08.110
the Evil God Case?

29:09.350 --> 29:11.410
Our first assignment in Balongzhou.

29:14.110 --> 29:14.770
No.

29:19.240 --> 29:20.630
Under the ancestral shrine
of that Evil God,

29:20.630 --> 29:22.230
there was a dying archivist—

29:22.420 --> 29:23.590
one of our own.

29:24.290 --> 29:25.290
He once told us:

29:25.880 --> 29:26.590
if we ever encounter a case

29:26.590 --> 29:28.450
related to reefs in the Archives,

29:28.530 --> 29:30.190
we must never investigate it,

29:32.000 --> 29:33.660
because it will get us killed.

29:35.000 --> 29:35.610
Really?

29:37.400 --> 29:38.660
Did he tell us not to go?

29:38.660 --> 29:39.330
He did.

29:39.330 --> 29:41.530
But what about the passengers who died?

29:42.030 --> 29:43.030
I'm going anyway.

29:50.330 --> 29:51.130
Alright then—

29:51.720 --> 29:52.350
look,

29:53.790 --> 29:54.610
this is your call.

29:54.610 --> 29:55.440
If you say go, we go;

29:55.440 --> 29:56.400
if you say don't, we don't.

29:56.400 --> 29:57.310
I'll follow you.

29:57.310 --> 29:59.240
I can't make that decision for you.

30:01.770 --> 30:03.010
Then let's go take a look.

30:03.010 --> 30:03.790
If anything

30:03.790 --> 30:04.750
feels wrong,

30:04.940 --> 30:06.800
we'll retreat if you say so, okay?

30:06.850 --> 30:07.910
We'll do as you say.

30:20.270 --> 30:21.070
Fine.

30:22.240 --> 30:23.110
You said so—

30:23.530 --> 30:24.660
you'll listen to me.

30:25.310 --> 30:26.640
Of course.

30:41.570 --> 30:42.350
Shrimpie,

30:43.330 --> 30:45.640
if we just keep sailing
in this direction,

30:45.640 --> 30:46.900
can we reach Xiacheng?

30:47.250 --> 30:49.180
You're standing on the wrong side.

30:49.420 --> 30:50.750
Xiacheng is over there.

30:56.640 --> 30:57.440
Stop smoking.

31:01.600 --> 31:04.340
[Chocolate]

31:01.980 --> 31:03.910
The smell will affect my judgment.

31:05.050 --> 31:05.980
Imported goods—

31:06.530 --> 31:07.750
this stuff is expensive.

31:07.750 --> 31:09.750
Since when did we get this well-off?

31:48.030 --> 31:49.090
Where's the ghost?

31:50.030 --> 31:50.550
I…

31:52.510 --> 31:53.680
to be honest,

31:54.220 --> 31:56.970
the last time I saw it
was in that thick fog.

31:57.310 --> 31:59.810
Once the mist cleared, it was gone.

31:59.810 --> 32:01.670
When does the fog usually come in?

32:02.030 --> 32:04.960
Normally, before sunset,

32:05.030 --> 32:06.890
the wind dies down

32:07.030 --> 32:08.920
and the fog slowly rolls in.

32:08.920 --> 32:10.500
It lasts until around midnight.

32:10.500 --> 32:11.790
When the wind picks up again,

32:11.790 --> 32:13.400
it clears everything away.

32:13.400 --> 32:15.900
That's when I saw the water ghost.

32:16.790 --> 32:17.960
Sun's about to set.

32:18.440 --> 32:19.110
Let's go.

32:24.480 --> 32:24.950
I…

32:27.590 --> 32:28.070
I…

32:30.680 --> 32:32.740
Bring the wine and the lanterns over.

32:32.780 --> 32:35.040
Then you're free to do whatever you want.

32:36.460 --> 32:37.490
But once I send the signal,

32:37.490 --> 32:38.410
if you're not here

32:38.410 --> 32:39.440
within 15 minutes,

32:39.440 --> 32:41.570
you can forget about staying in Balai.

32:59.660 --> 33:01.300
There's something strange here.

33:01.300 --> 33:02.700
It doesn't look natural—

33:02.770 --> 33:06.030
more like something's been
heavily scraped or gouged out.

33:15.640 --> 33:16.770
The fog's coming in.

34:34.690 --> 34:35.610
Shrimpie,

34:36.480 --> 34:39.739
the fog's rolling in.
We'd better coordinate our actions.

34:41.980 --> 34:43.380
Shrimpie, are you there?

34:43.460 --> 34:44.580
I'm here.

34:49.440 --> 34:50.440
What do you think?

34:50.610 --> 34:52.340
It's all the stench of corpses.

34:52.460 --> 34:54.790
Looks like they're definitely not alive.

34:56.750 --> 34:58.880
Should we regroup first or something?

34:59.790 --> 35:00.650
Are you scared?

35:02.930 --> 35:04.930
Can you stop picking a fight with me?

35:41.880 --> 35:42.940
Pickled…

35:44.550 --> 35:46.580
What, have people been pickling bodies

35:46.580 --> 35:48.180
all these years just for fun?

35:56.360 --> 35:57.230
Chen Libiao.

35:57.610 --> 35:58.060
Oh no!

35:58.400 --> 35:59.000
Shrimpie,

35:59.190 --> 36:00.320
Chen Libiao's dead!

36:03.000 --> 36:03.600
Shrimpie!

36:11.050 --> 36:11.900
You okay?

36:15.690 --> 36:17.290
A cut-off retreat like this—

36:17.460 --> 36:19.120
only humans could pull it off.

36:20.050 --> 36:21.510
Since it's not a haunting,

36:21.820 --> 36:23.630
there must be a ship nearby.

36:25.170 --> 36:26.600
Right now,

36:26.820 --> 36:28.280
they're trying to scare us

36:28.610 --> 36:30.670
into spreading rumors about ghosts.

36:31.030 --> 36:33.050
That means we can
definitely get out of here.

36:33.050 --> 36:34.550
What we need to do now

36:34.860 --> 36:35.610
is stay calm.

36:35.940 --> 36:37.530
All of you, come out!

36:39.150 --> 36:42.630
I am Zhang Salty, a commissioner of
the Nanyang Maritime Supervisory Office.

36:42.630 --> 36:44.430
If you're trying to play tricks,

36:45.190 --> 36:47.520
I will bring all of you to justice!

36:47.610 --> 36:48.380
Surrender within 3 minutes,

36:48.380 --> 36:49.710
and only the ringleader

36:49.880 --> 36:50.880
will be punished.

36:51.010 --> 36:54.780
After 3 minutes,
you will be executed on the spot!

36:58.300 --> 36:59.500
Don't talk nonsense.

36:59.900 --> 37:01.530
The 3 minutes aren't even up yet.

37:01.530 --> 37:02.760
You actually believed me?

37:02.760 --> 37:04.820
Hurry, scare them before they react!

37:21.260 --> 37:24.920
These look like the passengers
who went missing from those ships.

37:25.480 --> 37:27.940
They've all been turned
into dried corpses.

38:14.570 --> 38:15.230
Blood—

38:15.610 --> 38:16.470
we've hit them!

38:16.700 --> 38:18.160
So it really is human work.

38:24.400 --> 38:25.510
How boring.

38:26.730 --> 38:28.280
All the strange cases
we've handled in Nanyang lately—

38:28.280 --> 38:30.000
turn out they're all caused by people.

38:30.000 --> 38:31.260
I guess, in this world,

38:32.320 --> 38:35.580
the only ones who can "play ghosts"
are humans themselves.

38:40.280 --> 38:41.210
What's going on?

38:42.760 --> 38:43.820
The wind is coming.

38:45.790 --> 38:47.190
The fog is about to clear.

39:07.360 --> 39:08.670
They're actually

39:09.480 --> 39:13.030
kind of considerate, aren't they—
putting on all this ghostly showmanship.

39:13.030 --> 39:14.560
It's all smoke and mirrors.

39:15.820 --> 39:16.550
Once the fog clears,

39:16.550 --> 39:18.550
those bodies just vanish in a flash.

39:19.480 --> 39:20.540
Remarkable trick.

39:23.670 --> 39:24.760
Where could they possibly

39:24.760 --> 39:27.620
hide all the people and corpses
in such a short time?

39:29.440 --> 39:30.110
Shrimpie,

39:31.260 --> 39:31.940
can you use the blood

39:31.940 --> 39:33.540
to pinpoint their position?

39:34.590 --> 39:36.590
Blood isn't a reliable scent marker.

39:36.590 --> 39:38.190
It doesn't carry far enough—

39:40.250 --> 39:41.710
the sea wind is too strong,

39:42.150 --> 39:44.010
and the smell disperses quickly.

39:46.710 --> 39:48.570
But there is something we can use.

40:02.630 --> 40:05.160
The cigarettes have already
been stepped on,

40:06.420 --> 40:07.400
but I mixed in some agarwood incense.

40:07.400 --> 40:09.400
That stuff has strong penetration.

40:09.460 --> 40:10.150
Try it—

40:12.710 --> 40:14.070
take a sniff.

40:28.850 --> 40:30.180
I can't smell anything.

40:30.720 --> 40:32.850
Your mouth reeks of smoke and alcohol.

40:33.360 --> 40:34.590
Stay away from me.

41:07.480 --> 41:08.800
They're on the sea.

41:15.380 --> 41:17.030
So someone

41:17.030 --> 41:18.190
quickly transported the bodies
back onto a ship

41:18.190 --> 41:19.400
and left the reef?

41:20.960 --> 41:23.090
What kind of ship could move that fast?

41:23.590 --> 41:24.790
Maybe it's not a ship.

41:24.960 --> 41:26.490
It might be something else.

41:26.880 --> 41:27.730
Want to know what it is?

41:27.730 --> 41:28.860
Let's go take a look.

41:56.610 --> 41:59.740
[Rusheng]

41:58.030 --> 41:59.160
What a massive ship!

42:00.800 --> 42:03.270
Isn't this the passenger liner
that disappeared a year ago?

42:03.270 --> 42:03.500
[Two merchant ships vanish in the same
treacherous waters within two months.]

42:03.550 --> 42:04.030
[Coast guard search finds
only scattered wreckage.]

42:03.670 --> 42:04.840
Over 200 passengers vanished

42:04.100 --> 42:04.250
[Deadly reefs lurk
beneath the emerald waves]

42:04.300 --> 42:04.710
[The century-old legend
of vengeful spirits at Panhua Reef]

42:04.760 --> 42:05.320
[Mysterious waters swallow ships—
dark clouds gather over Nanyang route]

42:04.840 --> 42:06.510
along with it back then—
this is the one, right?

42:05.350 --> 42:06.100
[Panhua Reef Incident
Alerts Multiple Parties]

42:06.140 --> 42:07.030
[Foreign shippers call
for joint international investigation]

42:07.010 --> 42:08.380
Looks like all the ships

42:08.380 --> 42:10.110
that went missing around Panhua Reef

42:10.110 --> 42:12.370
over the past year have been hidden here.

42:12.480 --> 42:13.420
Who did this?

42:13.760 --> 42:14.960
And for what purpose?

42:15.300 --> 42:16.360
Whatever the case,

42:16.940 --> 42:18.380
this is definitely a major incident.

42:18.380 --> 42:18.910
Let's go.

42:25.800 --> 42:27.260
The two people on the reef—

42:27.360 --> 42:28.170
one of them

42:28.170 --> 42:30.070
claimed to be
from the Maritime Supervisory Office,

42:30.070 --> 42:31.920
but he didn't look like a member of it.

42:31.920 --> 42:33.320
He could even spit blades.

42:33.320 --> 42:34.760
No idea where he came from.

42:34.760 --> 42:36.030
No matter what faction they belong to,

42:36.030 --> 42:37.650
we don't take them seriously.

42:37.650 --> 42:39.310
Why are there warlords again?

42:40.280 --> 42:41.570
Look at those soldiers—

42:41.570 --> 42:43.920
they're all carrying
Denasien-made Mauser rifles.

42:43.920 --> 42:46.050
And that leader even has a Luger on him.

42:46.550 --> 42:48.690
These are weapons we can barely
even get close to.

42:48.690 --> 42:50.490
The soldier's rank is very high.

42:50.510 --> 42:52.900
Also, look at this chained formation—
it's very well planned.

42:52.900 --> 42:53.900
The guard positions on this ship

42:53.900 --> 42:56.760
are also clearly laid out
and tightly coordinated.

42:57.300 --> 43:00.960
And none of these sentries
are showing the slightest negligence.

43:02.610 --> 43:05.140
Whoever's behind this
is no ordinary person.

43:07.480 --> 43:08.410
You've grown up—

43:08.850 --> 43:10.380
you can analyze things now.

43:10.820 --> 43:12.760
Back then, I was always the one
doing the analysis.

43:12.760 --> 43:14.590
I make it sound cooler than you do.

43:14.590 --> 43:16.470
Let's go up and check.

43:17.000 --> 43:20.400
With something this big,
let's see what they're really up to.

43:27.150 --> 43:28.230
What's going on?

43:28.730 --> 43:30.330
Sir, one of the lights is out.

43:30.690 --> 43:32.090
Go check it immediately.

43:32.570 --> 43:33.420
Yes, sir.

43:35.670 --> 43:36.820
Stay on high alert.

43:37.210 --> 43:37.740
Yes, sir.

43:53.420 --> 43:54.130
Hurry up.

43:55.850 --> 43:56.340
Hey, you.

43:56.340 --> 43:58.320
These warlords are making
such a huge operation…

43:58.320 --> 43:59.960
just to dig a hole on the reef?

44:10.880 --> 44:11.600
Hurry up.

44:15.230 --> 44:16.230
What do you smell?

44:16.820 --> 44:17.960
There's a strange odor

44:17.960 --> 44:19.620
coming from inside that cave.

44:28.690 --> 44:30.670
So this is
where those "water ghosts" come from.

44:30.670 --> 44:33.520
Looks like these are
the missing passengers from those ships.

44:33.520 --> 44:34.690
If that's the case,

44:34.920 --> 44:37.250
they've been digging here
for a long time.

44:37.680 --> 44:39.380
What exactly is down in this reef?

44:39.380 --> 44:40.050
Go down now!

44:40.550 --> 44:41.350
Keep digging.

44:42.110 --> 44:43.580
The concentration down there
is even higher.

44:43.580 --> 44:45.460
Several people have already died.

44:45.460 --> 44:47.830
If we go down too, we'll die as well.

44:47.850 --> 44:49.270
Don't force us anymore.

44:50.730 --> 44:52.330
Let's go down and take a look.

44:52.690 --> 44:54.510
While we're at it,
take out a few of them.

44:54.510 --> 44:56.220
They've got numbers and firepower.

44:56.220 --> 44:57.550
Even if we take out a few,

44:57.570 --> 44:58.670
we can't save everyone.

44:58.670 --> 45:00.010
Stop looking. Just work.

45:00.010 --> 45:02.280
We need to figure out
what's down there first.

45:02.280 --> 45:03.480
Grab someone and question them.

45:03.480 --> 45:04.670
When I came up,

45:05.090 --> 45:07.210
I smelled signs that someone had been
living in the ship's cabin.

45:07.210 --> 45:08.170
There are people inside.

45:08.170 --> 45:10.500
What kind of strange smell
is it this time?

45:18.430 --> 45:19.760
Smells like cured meat.

45:22.070 --> 45:22.570
What's going on?

45:22.570 --> 45:23.360
What happened?

45:23.360 --> 45:25.090
Why did the lights go out again?

45:34.860 --> 45:36.920
They'll notice in less than a minute.

45:37.000 --> 45:38.400
Isn't one minute enough?

46:09.340 --> 46:11.800
What the hell are these soldiers
doing here?

46:12.250 --> 46:13.690
Playing tricks.

46:15.390 --> 46:17.120
See the threads on the corpses?

46:17.550 --> 46:19.080
If I'm not mistaken,

46:19.880 --> 46:22.340
these warlords
are using those steel cables

46:22.660 --> 46:25.110
to quickly bring the bodies out
to the edge of the reef—

46:25.110 --> 46:27.440
and then make them disappear just as fast.

46:28.150 --> 46:29.210
How does that work?

46:30.460 --> 46:32.920
Something like a sail-hoisting mechanism.

46:33.580 --> 46:36.710
They first use the fog
to bring the ship close to the reef,

46:37.280 --> 46:38.280
then operate

46:38.280 --> 46:39.630
a dome-like rig.

46:40.030 --> 46:41.020
By pulling the ropes,

46:41.020 --> 46:42.680
the bodies are made to appear,

46:43.590 --> 46:45.050
and then disappear again—

46:46.480 --> 46:48.030
just like raising

46:54.030 --> 46:55.510
and lowering a sail.

47:00.420 --> 47:02.150
You're quick on the uptake.

47:04.590 --> 47:06.190
But why would these soldiers

47:06.360 --> 47:08.820
use corpses to pull off
something like this?

47:09.210 --> 47:09.670
Go away.

47:09.980 --> 47:10.940
Clumsy idiot.

47:33.400 --> 47:34.730
The smell is extremely pungent—

47:34.730 --> 47:37.790
some kind of chemical solution,
I can't tell what it is.

47:39.590 --> 47:40.620
What is he doing?

47:50.110 --> 47:56.230
[Chen Xifeng,
Deputy Officer, Beilian Mo Faction]

47:50.880 --> 47:53.090
From Panhua Reef all the way here...

47:53.340 --> 47:54.670
Based on my assessment,

47:55.230 --> 47:57.780
ordinary people can't possibly
have swum this distance—

47:57.780 --> 47:59.510
except for Zhang Qishan's men.

47:59.920 --> 48:00.400
Hurry,

48:00.840 --> 48:02.610
everyone gets weapons ready.

48:03.010 --> 48:04.760
If they really were Zhang Qishan's men,

48:04.760 --> 48:06.810
we won't find them
just by searching like this.

48:06.810 --> 48:08.160
Today, we must—

48:17.070 --> 48:18.450
Shh…

48:18.480 --> 48:20.040
shh…

48:22.360 --> 48:22.760
Shh...

48:24.000 --> 48:25.480
If I let go, you're dead.

48:25.590 --> 48:26.210
Answer my questions,

48:26.210 --> 48:27.740
and I'll stitch you back up.

48:28.740 --> 48:29.700
Who are you?

48:29.720 --> 48:30.780
Where are you from?

48:30.900 --> 48:32.160
What's under the reef?

48:35.560 --> 48:37.210
The soldiers above
are about to come down.

48:37.210 --> 48:38.110
Think of something—

48:38.110 --> 48:38.910
draw them away

48:39.250 --> 48:40.590
and buy us some time.

48:47.260 --> 48:49.120
I think I've figured out
what's beneath the reef.

48:49.120 --> 48:50.690
Before the Ming Dynasty's maritime bans,

48:50.690 --> 48:52.050
people transported
countless rare treasures

48:52.050 --> 48:53.030
from the Persian Gulf region

48:53.030 --> 48:54.830
through the Maritime Silk Road—

48:54.840 --> 48:55.900
67 ships in total.

48:56.840 --> 48:58.700
These vessels sank during a storm

48:59.170 --> 49:01.170
while passing through Panhua Reef.

49:01.590 --> 49:03.610
Just look at those guys on the reef—

49:03.610 --> 49:04.320
you can tell

49:04.320 --> 49:06.450
they're not here for sunken treasure.

49:07.050 --> 49:09.310
There must be something else down there.

49:09.390 --> 49:09.630
[Report]

49:09.660 --> 49:10.260
[III. Test Conclusions]

49:13.050 --> 49:15.510
They're trying
to blow open the reef cavern.

49:16.150 --> 49:16.820
Blow it up?

49:17.740 --> 49:18.720
Good—

49:20.420 --> 49:21.340
then let's help them.

49:21.340 --> 49:22.050
Get more explosives

49:22.050 --> 49:22.900
and blow up the control room.

49:22.900 --> 49:23.690
Something's not right.

49:23.690 --> 49:26.150
Why haven't they
actually detonated it yet?

49:26.340 --> 49:27.670
Because they don't dare—

49:27.670 --> 49:28.630
they think something dangerous
is down there.

49:28.420 --> 49:30.650
[III. Test Conclusions]

49:29.900 --> 49:31.500
If there's
really something that dangerous,

49:31.500 --> 49:33.160
then even more reason
for us to blow it open.

49:33.160 --> 49:34.080
Go to the deck—

49:34.440 --> 49:36.370
check if they've moved to the deck.

49:36.630 --> 49:37.430
Don't forget.

49:38.240 --> 49:40.720
[Golden Needle—Special Equipment
of the Archives; Voice Modulation]

49:38.610 --> 49:39.980
There are hundreds of guns

49:39.980 --> 49:41.090
and hundreds of hostages on this ship.

49:41.090 --> 49:41.880
If we don't stir things up,

49:41.880 --> 49:43.800
there's no way
we're getting out of here.

49:43.800 --> 49:44.650
Check over there.

49:44.650 --> 49:45.000
Yes.

49:47.460 --> 49:49.020
From Panhua Reef all the way here...

49:49.020 --> 49:50.820
Ordinary people can't possibly
have swum this distance—

49:50.820 --> 49:52.550
except for Zhang Qishan's men.

49:54.520 --> 49:55.920
Think fast. Make a decision.

49:55.920 --> 49:56.850
There's no time.

49:57.610 --> 49:58.740
Let's take a gamble.

49:59.610 --> 50:00.740
It's worth the risk.

50:01.880 --> 50:03.280
You've made up your mind?

50:03.940 --> 50:05.740
Didn't you used to keep asking me

50:06.130 --> 50:08.330
what should be done and what shouldn't?

50:08.500 --> 50:09.500
I'll tell you now—

50:09.690 --> 50:10.420
this is

50:10.820 --> 50:11.690
worth the risk.

50:12.380 --> 50:13.650
But let me be clear:

50:14.050 --> 50:15.670
this is just a calculated risk,

50:15.670 --> 50:16.800
not a free-for-all.

50:17.820 --> 50:18.550
Don't worry.

50:18.740 --> 50:20.000
After all these years,

50:21.420 --> 50:23.080
I know how to restrain myself.

50:25.380 --> 50:27.510
You're already getting carried away.

50:33.880 --> 50:34.360
Come in.

50:40.980 --> 50:41.580
Adjutant,

50:41.670 --> 50:42.690
what's with the gunfire?

50:42.690 --> 50:43.330
Got it.

50:44.970 --> 50:46.360
Someone just infiltrated the room

50:46.360 --> 50:47.760
and has already escaped.

50:48.280 --> 50:49.340
Search the entire vessel.

50:49.340 --> 50:49.870
Yes, sir.

50:49.990 --> 50:50.590
By the way,

50:50.670 --> 50:52.130
what's the situation now?

50:52.210 --> 50:54.480
We're about to reach the lower cargo hold
of that sunken ship.

50:54.480 --> 50:55.760
We're proceeding with extreme caution—

50:55.760 --> 50:58.420
worried that whatever is inside
might come out.

50:59.680 --> 51:00.320
Good.

51:01.210 --> 51:02.070
Let me test you—

51:02.510 --> 51:04.650
if you're afraid something inside
might come out,

51:04.650 --> 51:06.650
what preparations should you make?

51:07.750 --> 51:10.010
Previously, we had the laborers
do the digging.

51:10.010 --> 51:11.600
We just cover our exposed skin

51:11.600 --> 51:13.630
and wear protective gear
soaked in chemical solution,

51:13.630 --> 51:14.460
and we're fine.

51:14.460 --> 51:15.610
Isn't that enough?

51:15.660 --> 51:16.970
The people who died over the past 2 years

51:16.970 --> 51:18.700
have all been handled this way,

51:18.850 --> 51:19.980
sealed with salt.

51:20.200 --> 51:21.810
We thought that was sufficient.

51:21.810 --> 51:22.880
Tell the men below—

51:22.950 --> 51:24.630
we must break through tonight.

51:24.630 --> 51:25.320
Speed it up.

51:25.730 --> 51:27.470
Zhang Qishan's men have arrived.

51:27.470 --> 51:28.000
Yes, sir.

51:29.170 --> 51:29.590
Wait.

51:35.150 --> 51:37.750
Have you ever heard
of a man called Zhang Salty?

51:39.280 --> 51:40.350
I'm not familiar, sir.

51:40.350 --> 51:42.510
You've never heard
of such a handsome man?

51:42.510 --> 51:43.500
He belongs

51:43.630 --> 51:47.340
to the Southern Archives under
the Nanyang Maritime Supervisory Office,

51:47.340 --> 51:50.170
specializing in investigating
strange phenomena across Nanyang.

51:50.170 --> 51:50.940
He is

51:51.070 --> 51:53.670
a world-class expert—

51:53.970 --> 51:55.430
how could you not know him?

51:55.630 --> 51:57.210
Let me tell you,

51:57.360 --> 51:59.220
his nickname is the "Sea Plague."

51:59.910 --> 52:00.950
This man

52:01.730 --> 52:03.580
is my lifelong rival.

52:05.230 --> 52:07.070
I've lived in his shadow

52:07.860 --> 52:09.130
for a long time.

52:14.120 --> 52:15.790
But given the current situation,

52:15.790 --> 52:18.050
I should explain things to you properly.

52:18.220 --> 52:19.050
Understood.

52:19.280 --> 52:20.500
But didn't you just say

52:20.500 --> 52:21.670
they were Zhang Qishan's men?

52:21.670 --> 52:23.000
This Zhang Salty is

52:23.000 --> 52:24.870
a thousand, ten thousand times
more troublesome than Zhang Qishan.

52:24.870 --> 52:26.270
I didn't tell you earlier

52:26.310 --> 52:28.560
because I was afraid
you'd wet your pants in fear.

52:28.560 --> 52:30.650
But now that he's infiltrated the ship,

52:30.650 --> 52:32.130
we're in serious trouble.

52:33.680 --> 52:35.540
So what does that mean, Adjutant?

52:36.110 --> 52:37.190
I am absolutely certain—

52:37.190 --> 52:39.090
Zhang Salty is already inside.

52:39.330 --> 52:40.860
He is extremely dangerous.

52:40.860 --> 52:42.210
If we don't complete the operation

52:42.210 --> 52:43.140
and blow it open,

52:43.210 --> 52:45.420
none of us will leave this place alive.

52:45.440 --> 52:45.970
Yes, sir.

52:46.240 --> 52:47.960
I'll send the laborers back down then.

52:47.960 --> 52:49.550
They're already beyond saving anyway—

52:49.550 --> 52:50.230
they'll die sooner or later.

52:50.230 --> 52:50.650
Idiot!

52:51.750 --> 52:52.870
You go down there yourselves.

52:52.870 --> 52:54.290
Keep the laborers away.

52:54.590 --> 52:56.000
I only trust you guys, understand?

52:56.000 --> 52:56.500
Yes, sir.

52:56.500 --> 52:57.360
Close the door.

53:15.800 --> 53:18.530
I think I've been
restraining myself quite well.

53:18.530 --> 53:19.140
Shrimpie,

53:19.380 --> 53:20.380
sometimes being too disciplined

53:20.380 --> 53:21.440
isn't a good thing.

53:21.760 --> 53:23.080
If you had lectured me
like that just now,

53:23.080 --> 53:24.810
I would've kicked you already—

53:25.010 --> 53:27.010
how could I have let that trick work?

53:27.460 --> 53:28.060
Of course,

53:28.570 --> 53:29.740
it's also hard
for normal people to believe

53:29.740 --> 53:31.290
someone could have such a thick skin.

53:31.290 --> 53:33.890
I admit I do have some talent
in that regard.

53:34.650 --> 53:36.340
You just got carried away again.

53:36.340 --> 53:37.440
It's going to be blown up anyway.

53:37.440 --> 53:40.640
If I didn't exaggerate a bit,
would they have believed it?

53:40.750 --> 53:42.860
Let's go check
what equipment we've got—

53:42.860 --> 53:44.390
we're going down there too.

53:47.560 --> 53:48.350
[Report]

53:48.370 --> 53:52.480
[Resembles a dandelion]

53:50.940 --> 53:51.820
Toxic weed—

53:52.010 --> 53:53.280
shaped like a dandelion.

53:52.550 --> 53:53.690
[Highly toxic weed—grows extremely fast]

53:53.510 --> 53:55.030
Contact causes immediate death

53:53.730 --> 53:54.840
[Contact develops
red rashes all over the body.]

53:54.900 --> 53:56.510
[Within half an hour,
the skin and flesh begin to rot.]

53:55.460 --> 53:56.780
or delayed death.

54:19.310 --> 54:20.190
Zhang Hailou,

54:20.940 --> 54:22.780
you'd better withdraw your order.

54:22.780 --> 54:23.580
What's wrong?

54:25.350 --> 54:26.890
This girl died of poisoning.

54:26.890 --> 54:29.240
The salt and chemical solution
were used for disinfection.

54:29.240 --> 54:30.690
If that's the case,

54:31.030 --> 54:32.270
those laborers also died
from this same poison—

54:32.270 --> 54:33.180
dying suddenly on the spot,

54:33.180 --> 54:35.580
which is why they were preserved
with salt.

54:36.830 --> 54:37.940
No wonder that guy said

54:37.940 --> 54:39.710
those laborers were beyond saving.

54:39.710 --> 54:40.680
They are poisoned.

54:40.680 --> 54:41.810
Look at this report—

54:43.210 --> 54:43.940
the toxin comes

54:43.940 --> 54:45.170
from a plant called "Twilight Grass."

54:45.170 --> 54:46.430
If it touches the skin,

54:46.430 --> 54:47.140
it causes ulceration

54:47.140 --> 54:48.130
and eventually leads to death.

54:48.130 --> 54:49.200
If inhaled directly,

54:49.200 --> 54:50.350
it leads to sudden death
on the spot.

54:50.350 --> 54:52.880
That's why the soldiers
kept killing people,

54:53.550 --> 54:54.810
then hijacking ships,

54:55.540 --> 54:56.900
forcing them to continue mining the reef.

54:55.770 --> 54:59.140
[Zhili Pill,
Secret Antidote of the Zhang Family]

54:56.920 --> 54:57.780
So

54:58.400 --> 54:59.820
what they dug out of that sunken ship

54:59.820 --> 55:00.890
wasn't some monster—

55:00.890 --> 55:01.620
it was…

55:03.530 --> 55:04.730
Twilight Grass.

55:08.350 --> 55:09.310
It's broken through!

55:09.310 --> 55:10.710
We've blown it open!

55:17.690 --> 55:19.220
Did I just cause a disaster?

55:19.810 --> 55:20.790
You're right—

55:20.810 --> 55:22.150
either way, we're dead.

55:22.300 --> 55:23.820
Time to clean up this mess.

55:24.560 --> 55:25.810
If we don't go to hell,

55:26.190 --> 55:27.230
who will?

55:29.510 --> 55:31.250
Then let's go all in.
